/*eslint-disable*/import type{Messages}from"@lingui/core";export const messages=JSON.parse("{\"-C4dIk\":[\"Boards that need a forcing chain are rare and expensive to search for on demand, so Suuudokuuu ships a bundled corpus that has already been checked by a Dancing Links exact-cover solver and a bitmask solver, rated, and filtered to forcing-chain boards before it is packed.\"],\"-Elizp\":[\"When intersections start feeling automatic, move up to the <0>printable Hard sudoku booklet</0> for fish and wing patterns. Drop back to <1>printable Easy sudoku</1> for a singles-only warm-up, or play Medium on a screen at the <2>Medium sudoku lander</2>.\"],\"-bYKwe\":[\"Includes Everest (SE 11.9), Platinum Blonde (SE 10.9) and AI Escargot (SE 10.6).\"],\"-iJ7nh\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, solvable with full houses and naked singles alone.\"],\"-vAdwL\":[\"Techniques\"],\"0Ktk6B\":[\"Updated <0>\",[\"formattedDate\"],\"</0>\"],\"0L9JZJ\":[\"How many puzzles are in the printable Easy sudoku PDF?\"],\"0MRfHz\":[\"Infinity Sudoku\"],\"0RoXsf\":[\"Is the printable Nightmare sudoku PDF free?\"],\"0Sy9Gs\":[\"How many puzzles are in the printable Hell sudoku PDF?\"],\"0bpi83\":[\"Printable sudoku booklets by difficulty\"],\"0r_rbI\":[\"Does \",[\"SITE_NAME\"],\" have ads?\"],\"0zmlwH\":[\"Download \",[\"title\"],\" (PDF)\"],\"18cwop\":[\"<0>Easy</0> — \",[\"easyClueCount\"],\" clues, guaranteed to need at least one hidden single and never more than that.\"],\"1KnfS2\":[\"How many clues does a Nightmare sudoku have?\"],\"1Lvcgc\":[\"Puzzle 1 from the Nightmare booklet, one of \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" in the PDF.\"],\"1SEI1B\":[\"It is Suuudokuuu’s hardest generated tier, measured at SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\" across a sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" boards. Every one of them needs chain or coloring logic on top of the fish and wing patterns Hard already requires.\"],\"1ZWQlV\":[\"How to print these puzzles\"],\"1ZluOW\":[\"Why paper helps with chains\"],\"1aVkEA\":[\"An intersection technique works on the overlap between one box and one row or column. A pointing pair or pointing triple finds a digit confined to two or three cells of a box that all share a line, and erases it from the rest of that line; box line reduction is the mirror image, working from a line back into a box. Naked and hidden pairs are the entry point to subset reasoning: two cells that share exactly two candidates, or two digits that fit in exactly two cells of a unit, either way locking those two cells away from everything else in it. None of these place a digit outright — they only eliminate candidates — but at \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues a Medium puzzle always has at least one waiting, and it is usually enough to unlock a fresh naked single a move or two later. The tier is capped at the other end too: nothing in it ever needs a fish, a wing or a chain, because a board that does is promoted to Hard instead.\"],\"27Qok0\":[\"Nothing in the tier ever needs a fish, a wing or a chain — a board that does is promoted to Hard instead.\"],\"2Dg4GX\":[\"How hard is it, honestly\"],\"2Ic_Zv\":[\"Free online sudoku means playing the classic 9×9 number puzzle in a browser or app with no purchase, install limit or paywall, and \",[\"SITE_NAME\"],\" is a free, open-source implementation of it — seven difficulty levels from Newbie to Infinity, technique-explaining guides, no ads and no tracking in the game. Solve in the browser or install the app; your progress, streaks and stats stay on the device you play on. See <0>why \",[\"SITE_NAME\"],\" is built this way</0> for the full, verifiable case.\"],\"2Lb_CG\":[\"Look for hidden singles\"],\"2N-XHb\":[\"Sudoku for seniors\"],\"2gnUkr\":[\"Newbie\"],\"2wuXBd\":[\"The very first thing to check is whether a box, row or column is missing only one digit. If eight of the nine cells in a unit are already filled, the ninth cell must take the digit the unit is still missing — no candidates to compare, just subtraction.\"],\"3-aLmy\":[\"Yes. Both are in the Infinity set, along with Platinum Blonde and Golden Nugget. Each game reshuffles digits, rows and columns, so the grid looks different every time while the puzzle stays the same.\"],\"35wRk8\":[\"It is the easiest tier Suuudokuuu offers, and the generator guarantees it: a board only ships as Newbie once a solver limited to full houses and naked singles has finished it. Our sample measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\", with no candidate tracking and no risk of a forced guess.\"],\"367Cn7\":[\"What technique does an Easy sudoku booklet require?\"],\"3DJmkH\":[\"Our technique engine agrees that these boards sit past its reach. It knows every pattern on the <0>technique index</0>, up to the <1/> and the <2/>, and it still cannot finish a single Infinity puzzle on its own. That does not mean they need guessing; it means they need longer forcing nets than the engine implements. Hints are off by default on Nightmare, Hell and Infinity, and a setting turns them back on if you want the engine’s help for as far as it goes.\"],\"3SwmIF\":[\"When you start an Infinity game, the app picks one of those puzzles and disguises it. It relabels the digits, shuffles rows within their bands, columns within their stacks and the bands and stacks themselves, and sometimes mirrors the grid across its diagonal. None of that changes the logic or the rating, so the Everest you play is still Everest, it just does not look like the picture below.\"],\"3a3AKD\":[\"Is this printable Newbie sudoku booklet free?\"],\"3c-rtT\":[\"Download on the App Store\"],\"3l9jCt\":[\"How many sudoku difficulty levels does Suuudokuuu have?\"],\"3m4lq2\":[\"A fish is easy to miss on a screen where only a handful of cells are visible at once, because the pattern lives in where one digit can go across two, three or four whole lines at the same time. On a full printed grid you can mark that digit’s remaining positions down a column and read the shape off the page. Wings need the opposite view — a few bivalue cells that see each other across the grid — and circling them in pencil makes the overlap obvious. Because both families are easy to apply incorrectly the first few times, checking your work against the solution pages at the back is worth doing every time until the shape becomes automatic.\"],\"4-X0DJ\":[\"Get it on Google Play\"],\"4DuWbm\":[\"<0>Row rule.</0> Each of the nine rows must contain the digits 1 to 9 exactly once each.\"],\"4EAgIb\":[\"Blank Sudoku Grid\"],\"4HAVnv\":[\"Every puzzle in this booklet comes from a bundled corpus that Suuudokuuu checks with two independent solving algorithms — a Dancing Links exact-cover solver and a typed-array bitmask solver — before it ships, so each grid is confirmed to have exactly one solution. The corpus draws from the tdoku project’s 17-clue catalog and the magictour top1465 hard-puzzle list, and each puzzle is also solved logically and rated on the SE scale as the corpus is packed. Only boards whose hardest step is a forcing chain survive; anything that falls to a chain, coloring or AIC is dropped, because neither the clue count nor the source list alone would be enough to promise a Hell puzzle. Every survivor still solves on our technique ladder without guessing, so every puzzle here is guaranteed solvable by logic before you ever pick up a pencil.\"],\"4NMPvd\":[\"What techniques do I need for Hard sudoku?\"],\"4apI84\":[\"Large print sudoku, printable\"],\"4gZ5Vw\":[\"Free and open source under the \",[\"SITE_LICENSE\"],\" license. No ads, no account, no tracking in the game — read <0>why</0> or browse the <1>full source on GitHub</1>. Apple and the Apple logo are trademarks of Apple Inc., registered in the U.S. and other countries. App Store is a service mark of Apple Inc. Google Play and the Google Play logo are trademarks of Google LLC.\"],\"52_TbA\":[\"Verifying fish and wings on paper\"],\"57DMl6\":[\"Chains falling into place? The <0>printable Hell sudoku booklet</0> is the last tier, where every puzzle needs a forcing chain. Step back to <1>printable Hard sudoku</1> for fish and wings only, or play Nightmare on a screen at the <2>Nightmare sudoku lander</2>.\"],\"5D6pgW\":[\"An Easy board from the same generator the app uses. Play it right here.\"],\"5EmtkG\":[\"Is the printable Hell sudoku PDF free?\"],\"5YPKNQ\":[\"Who rated these puzzles?\"],\"5a2b2H\":[\"Are these 17-clue puzzles?\"],\"5tWoLs\":[\"Learn sudoku\"],\"64gfbY\":[\"Play Newbie Sudoku now\"],\"6JHmjr\":[\"Yes. Every grid is checked by a Dancing Links exact-cover solver and a bitmask solver before it ships, and each has exactly one solution.\"],\"6Y2zqp\":[\"Is Medium sudoku hard?\"],\"6i2Miv\":[\"Nightmare holds just \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues, and it is the booklet where the printed page genuinely earns its keep. Every puzzle in it was tested against a solver that already knows every fish and wing — including the <0>swordfish</0> and the <1>XY-Wing</1> — and kept only because that solver stalled. What finishes them is chain reasoning, and a chain is far easier to build on paper, where you can pencil the links in and follow them, than on a cramped screen. Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" boards measures the tier at SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\".\"],\"6mE7Xy\":[\"An intersection or a pair only becomes visible once you can see every remaining candidate in a row, column or box at a glance, which is why paper genuinely helps here more than a screen does: write small digits in the corner of each blank cell, then scan a line for a digit trapped inside one box, or two cells sharing exactly two candidates between them. Neither pattern places a digit by itself — each one only removes candidates — so expect to mark a few eliminations before a fresh naked single actually appears. Working in pencil rather than pen means a wrong mark costs nothing to erase.\"],\"6pYHox\":[\"<0>Newbie.</0> Solvable with full houses and naked singles alone.\"],\"6tfEbk\":[\"Every board is checked for exactly one solution by two independent solving algorithms.\"],\"6yBCvI\":[\"What makes a puzzle Nightmare\"],\"6z6usR\":[\"Want the record puzzles on paper? Download the <0>printable Infinity sudoku PDF</0>. Not ready for them yet? Step back to <1>Hell Sudoku</1>, where every board needs a forcing chain but stays within reach of our technique ladder. Read the stories behind Everest and AI Escargot on the <2>hardest sudoku puzzles</2> page, compare every tier on the <3>Sudoku difficulty levels</3> hub, or head <4>home</4>.\"],\"6zwJ5l\":[\"Easy sits at the bottom of the SE (Sudoku Explainer) scale alongside Newbie: our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\". The two tiers share a range because SE prices a hidden single at 1.5, below a naked single at 2.3 — so the technique that defines Easy is, by that scale, cheaper than the one that defines Newbie. What genuinely changes is where you have to look: a naked single is read off one cell, a hidden single off a whole unit. It suits players who have cleared a few Newbie boards and want a puzzle that takes noticeably longer to finish.\"],\"75Y3_I\":[\"Is AI Escargot in the printable booklet?\"],\"7A3Fmz\":[\"Easier difficulty\"],\"7Y8jud\":[\"Play Hard Sudoku now\"],\"7Z44bB\":[\"Spotting fish and wings reliably? Move up to the <0>printable Nightmare sudoku booklet</0> for chains and coloring. Step back to <1>printable Medium sudoku</1> for intersections and subsets only, or play Hard on a screen at the <2>Hard sudoku lander</2>.\"],\"7hktsm\":[\"Getting started\"],\"7lhqPv\":[\"TL;DR\"],\"7r6sCa\":[\"Text size\"],\"7z1tpm\":[\"No. Notes mode in an app tracks candidates for you, updates them automatically as you place digits, and lets you undo a mistake without erasing.\"],\"83yMJR\":[\"Every tier from Newbie to Infinity now has its own guide, breaking down exactly what separates one level from the next — clue counts, required techniques and an honest read on how hard each one really is. Start on the <0>Sudoku difficulty levels</0> hub, or see how it compares to the <1>hardest puzzles</1> ever published.\"],\"8GGOmr\":[\"A finished grid satisfies all three at the same time. That overlap is what makes Sudoku solvable by logic: a digit that is already ruled out by its row, its column and its box has nowhere left to go, which is the basis of almost every solving technique. Every named technique on this site, from the simplest single to the longest chain, is ultimately just a more efficient way of tracking that overlap across many cells at once instead of one cell at a time.\"],\"8HgdwA\":[[\"mediumClueCount\"],\" clues, guaranteed to stall on singles and to yield to intersections and subsets. See the <0>Medium sudoku lander</0> to play it digitally.\"],\"8hKEc0\":[\"Nightmare Sudoku FAQ\"],\"8j_b89\":[\"Nightmare is capped at AIC — a board resisting that is beyond what the generated tiers hand you.\"],\"8ko6ZU\":[\"<0>Hell</0> — guaranteed to stall on AIC and to need a forcing chain, drawn from a bundled, verified corpus rather than generated to a band.\"],\"8wCnRb\":[\"The puzzles are printed exactly as they were published, with no reshuffling, so you can compare your grid with the originals discussed on the <0>hardest sudoku puzzles</0> page. They print \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page with room for a full set of pencil marks, which you will need: at this level most solvers keep every candidate written in and test chains on a separate sheet. The final pages hold the completed grids, so you can check a long line of reasoning without having to finish it first.\"],\"92GEeo\":[\"Want to warm up first? The <0>printable Hell sudoku booklet</0> holds forcing-chain puzzles that are hard but still within reach of our technique ladder. Prefer a screen? Play the same record puzzles on the <1>Infinity sudoku lander</1>, where each game reshuffles the grid, or browse every booklet on the <2>printable sudoku hub</2>.\"],\"93EF2k\":[\"How many clues does a Hell sudoku have?\"],\"9AexDe\":[\"A board that a full-house-and-naked-single solver can finish is rejected as too easy for the tier.\"],\"9COcEj\":[\"Fish patterns: X-Wing, swordfish, jellyfish and their finned and sashimi variants. Wing patterns: XY-Wing, XYZ-Wing and W-Wing.\"],\"9TF92W\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Easy boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\".\"],\"9e_cYH\":[\"Newbie Sudoku FAQ\"],\"9qTjdv\":[\"How many puzzles are in the printable Medium sudoku PDF?\"],\"9rfjS-\":[[\"PRINTABLE_LARGE_PRINT_PAGE_COUNT\"],\" pages\"],\"AKA0Xn\":[\"What techniques does this Hard booklet require?\"],\"AV85q_\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, solved start to finish with full houses, naked singles and hidden singles.\"],\"AdsNQX\":[\"Yes. Our sample measures Hell at SE \",[\"hellSeRatingRange\"],\", and every Infinity puzzle carries a published rating between \",[\"lowestRatingLabel\"],\" and \",[\"highestRatingLabel\"],\". Hell boards still yield to our technique ladder; Infinity boards do not.\"],\"AfMtNM\":[\"Hell Sudoku FAQ\"],\"Ak9Eh5\":[\"A Hard board from the same generator the app uses. Play it right here.\"],\"B-pBHn\":[\"Sudoku difficulty chain\"],\"BJrGt8\":[\"Exactly one technique. Every Newbie board can be finished with full houses and naked singles; every Easy board provably cannot, and needs at least one hidden single to break the deadlock.\"],\"BZz12Q\":[\"Print\"],\"C1_WBQ\":[\"Sudoku is a logic puzzle played on a 9×9 grid, divided into nine 3×3 boxes. The goal is to fill every empty cell with a digit from 1 to 9 so that no digit repeats in any row, column or box. A well-formed Sudoku always starts with some cells already filled in — the givens, or clues — and always has exactly one valid solution reachable by logic alone, with no guessing.\"],\"C4kvBI\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Hell boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\", with the <0/> as the most common hardest step.\"],\"CA7v0X\":[\"Some of these grids start with as few as \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MINIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" givens and look almost empty at first glance — the \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles print \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page with generous cell size specifically so there is room to track candidates by hand across a long chain. The final pages hold the completed grids, which is close to essential at this tier: verifying a chain of eliminations by eye is slow, and a printed key lets you confirm the end state without re-deriving the whole path.\"],\"CAD1qm\":[\"A chain follows an alternating sequence of strong and weak links, starting from a candidate and working outward until it proves an elimination or a placement no matter which branch turns out to be true. X-Chain works on a single digit; XY-Chain follows a path of bivalue cells instead. Simple coloring assigns two alternating colours to a network of strong links on one digit and clears any candidate that sees both colours, and AIC generalises the whole family, mixing digits and cell types along one continuous chain. Hell starts where all of that runs out. A forcing chain assumes a candidate, a cell’s possibilities or a house’s placements, follows every consequence, and keeps only what holds in every branch — the <0>Nishio</0>, <1>cell</1> and <2>region forcing chain</2> pages walk through one of each. A board makes the Hell corpus only if its hardest step on the rating-optimal path is a forcing chain, and only if our ladder can still finish it, so no Hell board ever asks you to guess.\"],\"CLPF0E\":[\"The ratings are the values independent raters publish, not our own measurements.\"],\"ChsZzh\":[[\"hardClueCount\"],\" clues, guaranteed to stall on subsets and to yield to fish and wing patterns. See the <0>Hard sudoku lander</0> to play it digitally.\"],\"DE2rA9\":[\"Clues versus difficulty\"],\"DE6q1A\":[\"Yes, by construction. Nightmare stops at AIC, and no Hell board can be solved with anything Nightmare allows. Our sample measures Hell at SE \",[\"hellSeRatingRange\"],\" and Nightmare at SE \",[\"nightmareSeRatingRange\"],\".\"],\"DFi0Zn\":[\"Harder than anything else in the app, by a wide margin. Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" <0>Hell</0> boards measures SE \",[\"hellSeRatingRange\"],\"; Infinity starts at \",[\"lowestRatingLabel\"],\". The Infinity ratings are not our own measurements. Suuudokuuu’s rater prices the SE ladder only as far as forcing chains and nets and reports \",[\"SE_RATING_CEILING\"],\" with a ceiling flag above that, so for these puzzles we quote the figures independent raters publish, as the <1>difficulty rating guide</1> explains.\"],\"DIr2XR\":[\"Intersections: pointing pair, pointing triple, box line reduction. Subsets: naked pair, hidden pair.\"],\"DRVEbn\":[\"Printable Hell Sudoku FAQ\"],\"DRleO8\":[\"<0>Full House</0> — the simplest possible move, filling the last empty cell in a unit.\"],\"D_b_9m\":[\"Easy Sudoku FAQ\"],\"DgPHNt\":[\"An almost-fish: the rows or columns line up as an X-Wing or <0>swordfish</0> except for one or two extra candidates, the fin. The elimination still holds, but only in the cells that both the fish and the fin can see.\"],\"DjGWF0\":[\"Pencil in every remaining candidate for the blank cells that are left, then work through the technique index in difficulty order to keep clearing them.\"],\"Drd4wO\":[\"A digit confined to two cells of one box that also share a row or column. It can then be erased from the rest of that row or column, since one of those two cells must hold it.\"],\"DvhSrh\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, guaranteed to need a hidden single and nothing harder.\"],\"E5Cz6q\":[[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles\"],\"ER15gL\":[\"An Infinity record puzzle from the same curated set the app uses, reshuffled. Play it right here.\"],\"ETZyJl\":[\"Seven difficulty levels from Newbie through Hell to Infinity, the top tier serving record puzzles such as Everest and AI Escargot\"],\"EYQUVy\":[\"<0>Hard.</0> Always stalls on subsets and always yields to a fish or a wing pattern.\"],\"EYVt4M\":[\"Largest text size\"],\"EyMkmB\":[\"What is the easiest Sudoku difficulty?\"],\"FfmJIb\":[\"Is the printable Medium sudoku PDF free?\"],\"Fgi0TQ\":[\"Nothing in the booklet needs a fish, a wing or a chain.\"],\"Fv02gG\":[\"Our published sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Hard boards measures the tier at SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\", with the <0/> as the most common hardest step — numbers the <1>sudoku difficulty rating guide</1> measures directly rather than assumes. The \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles here print \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page with room to mark candidates, and the solved grids on the closing pages let you confirm a fish elimination actually held.\"],\"G70CkD\":[\"How many clues does a Medium sudoku have?\"],\"GCBW83\":[\"Solve the cheapest placements first: full houses, then naked singles, then hidden singles.\"],\"GOSVU9\":[\"Medium boards carry \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues and are guaranteed to stall on singles and yield to an intersection or a subset.\"],\"GRoZ7D\":[\"Hell Sudoku\"],\"GU9wm2\":[\"Can I use them in a classroom?\"],\"G_3WRn\":[\"Does it work offline?\"],\"GalvXV\":[\"Infinity is Suuudokuuu’s tier beyond Hell: a curated set of the hardest sudoku puzzles ever published, the record grids the solving community still argues about, ready to play for free. Every Infinity board is a known puzzle with a published Sudoku Explainer (SE) rating of at least \",[\"minimumRatingLabel\"],\" — Arto Inkala’s Everest, Platinum Blonde, AI Escargot, Golden Nugget and \",[\"additionalPuzzleCount\"],\" more — checked for a single solution before it ships. These are the puzzles our <0>hardest sudoku puzzles</0> guide describes; Infinity is where you play them.\"],\"GeGHUl\":[\"Every PDF is set to US Letter and drawn with vector lines and text, so it prints crisply at any size. Open the file, print at 100% scale (not “fit to page”, which can distort the grid on some printers), and print single-sided if you want to keep the solutions on separate sheets from the puzzles.\"],\"Gfmra_\":[\"An Easy board to start with. Play it right here, or pick any of seven difficulty levels in the app.\"],\"Gu8Ueq\":[\"What makes a puzzle Infinity\"],\"GzaiWG\":[\"How to play Sudoku FAQ\"],\"H47ltZ\":[\"How do I print these puzzles?\"],\"HCMGUO\":[\"Do you ever have to guess?\"],\"HDn1fw\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, guaranteed to need at least one fish or wing pattern beyond every subset.\"],\"HJEQpI\":[\"Anywhere from \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MINIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" to \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MAXIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\". Hell does not use clue count to choose its puzzles; a board qualifies by needing a forcing chain, whatever its number of givens.\"],\"HPogd9\":[\"Why is paper recommended for chain-based puzzles?\"],\"HQCVxF\":[\"Is Newbie the right level for a child or a first-time solver?\"],\"HSXkrR\":[\"A well-formed puzzle always has exactly one solution and never requires a guess.\"],\"HV3Yoi\":[\"Hard Sudoku\"],\"Ht078b\":[\"Puzzle 1 from the Medium booklet, one of \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" in the PDF.\"],\"I11j00\":[\"Nightmare is Suuudokuuu’s expert tier — what most other apps would call very hard or expert. A Nightmare board carries just \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, and it is the tier where bounded patterns stop being enough: every board here has been checked against a solver that already knows every fish and every wing up to the <0>W-Wing</0>, and is only labelled Nightmare because that solver stalled. Finishing one needs chain reasoning — <1>X-Chain</1>, <2>XY-Chain</2>, <3>simple coloring</3> and <4>AIC</4>, the alternating inference chain that generalises the other three.\"],\"I3XIAf\":[\"Prefer a screen? Play Suuudokuuu now\"],\"IANVSf\":[\"No. There are no ads anywhere and no tracking inside the game; this website uses only cookieless, anonymous page analytics.\"],\"IB9N-i\":[\"What is the difference between a clue and a candidate?\"],\"IFKUNe\":[\"No pencil marks, no elimination logic and no guessing required for any puzzle in the booklet.\"],\"IOgWqm\":[\"Loading the board…\"],\"IjDWTu\":[\"How the puzzles are verified\"],\"IlAsp5\":[\"Which sudoku difficulty should I start with?\"],\"IqBsZ0\":[\"Yes. The PDF downloads free, with no account and no watermark, and includes a full solution key for every puzzle.\"],\"IrAE3z\":[\"Solver\"],\"Iu83qB\":[\"Puzzle 1 from the Newbie booklet, one of \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" in the PDF.\"],\"JBdo3D\":[\"Sudoku difficulty levels FAQ\"],\"JJoC7U\":[\"What makes a puzzle Hard\"],\"Jrqsp5\":[\"Hardness here comes from the technique each board requires, not from the clue count.\"],\"JrrSQM\":[\"What is the difference between Newbie and Easy sudoku?\"],\"Jry7J2\":[\"A Newbie board from the same generator the app uses. Play it right here.\"],\"KDXdKh\":[\"A Nightmare board from the same generator the app uses. Play it right here.\"],\"KPuUq2\":[\"Write in candidates once the easy cells run out\"],\"KQe27c\":[\"Are the solutions included?\"],\"KVC9CP\":[\"The printable Newbie Sudoku booklet is a free PDF of \",[\"clueCount\"],\"-clue puzzles where every blank is reachable with a full house or a naked single — a property each puzzle was checked for before it went into the PDF. It is the booklet to hand a first-time solver, a classroom just learning the rules, or anyone who wants a puzzle that never demands a second guess.\"],\"KiwVTj\":[\"Does Suuudokuuu offer a large-print version of this booklet?\"],\"Kmcrz2\":[\"Yes. \",[\"SITE_NAME\"],\" is free and open source, with no in-app purchases, subscriptions or paywalled difficulty levels.\"],\"L0XezG\":[\"What makes a puzzle Hell\"],\"L36iW5\":[\"Yes. Suuudokuuu’s code, including the generator behind these puzzles, is open source under the MIT license, and this site places no restriction on printing or redistributing the PDFs — including handing them out in a classroom, a tutoring session or a worksheet packet.\"],\"L3TeBG\":[\"How hard is Newbie sudoku?\"],\"LBVuWJ\":[\"Newbie Sudoku\"],\"LDOq68\":[\"How many puzzles are in the printable Nightmare sudoku PDF?\"],\"LI4SwS\":[\"What makes a puzzle Medium\"],\"LNoRL7\":[\"<0>Easy.</0> Adds hidden singles, still no candidate tracking required.\"],\"LfQJwZ\":[\"A cover page states the puzzle and page counts up front, then \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles print \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page so a single sheet holds \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" complete grids. The last pages hold every solved grid at the same layout, so checking an answer never means hunting through a different page format. The whole file is vector graphics and a standard PDF font, so it prints cleanly at any size a printer supports. Our published sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Easy boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\" — numbers the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0> measures directly rather than assumes.\"],\"LrHydF\":[\"Read the <0>how to play guide</0> for the three rules and a walkthrough of your first moves, or look up any term in the <1>sudoku glossary</1>, which defines every technique and every piece of vocabulary the guides use.\"],\"Lxq-zS\":[\"Large Print Sudoku\"],\"M1Yfw6\":[\"At least one <0>hidden single</0> per puzzle, on top of the full houses and naked singles Newbie already uses, and nothing harder.\"],\"MLFx1h\":[\"Yes. Easy is the source tier for the large-print PDF, sampled at \",[\"PRINTABLE_LARGE_PRINT_SIZE\"],\" puzzles with bigger cells for readers who want more room to write.\"],\"MREaAq\":[\"Everything Medium needs, plus at least one fish or wing pattern: X-Wing, swordfish, jellyfish, their finned and sashimi variants, XY-Wing, XYZ-Wing or W-Wing. One of those is always required, because a board that does not need one is graded Medium instead.\"],\"MVYMfh\":[\"Sudoku difficulties\"],\"M_zq3f\":[\"Printable Infinity Sudoku FAQ\"],\"Mz7rRO\":[\"Check every row, column and box for one that already has eight of its nine cells filled, and place the missing digit in the empty one.\"],\"N0hmpU\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells — only one fewer than Medium, which is exactly why the tier is defined by the techniques it requires rather than by its clue count.\"],\"NQTfla\":[\"Printable Newbie Sudoku FAQ\"],\"NeWjyh\":[\"<0>Newbie</0> — \",[\"newbieClueCount\"],\" clues, solved with full houses and naked singles alone.\"],\"NkdmkS\":[\"What techniques does this Nightmare booklet require?\"],\"Nq65SI\":[\"No. Clue count and difficulty are separate facts — see the <0>17-clue sudoku guide</0>. These puzzles are hard because every one needs a forcing chain, not because of how many clues they start with.\"],\"NuoZju\":[\"Finished a Hell board and want more? <0>Infinity Sudoku</0> serves the record puzzles — Everest, Platinum Blonde, AI Escargot — that sit past even our forcing chains. Not ready for chains yet? Step back to <1>Nightmare Sudoku</1>, which asks for the same reasoning with more of the grid already filled in. Prefer paper? Download the <2>printable Hell sudoku PDF</2>. Browse the <3>technique index</3>, especially X-Chain, XY-Chain, Simple Coloring and AIC, the <4>how to play guide</4>, the <5>17-clue sudoku guide</5>, every tier on the <6>Sudoku difficulty levels</6> hub, or head <7>home</7>.\"],\"Nyd-0x\":[\"How many clues does a Hard sudoku have?\"],\"NzFVBG\":[\"How is a fish or wing easier to verify on paper?\"],\"OMs2n2\":[\"Ready to chain eliminations together instead of spotting shapes? Move up to <0>Nightmare Sudoku</0>, or step back to <1>Medium Sudoku</1> for an intersections-and-subsets puzzle. Prefer paper? Download the <2>printable Hard sudoku PDF</2>. See the <3>technique index</3>, the <4>how to play guide</4>, every tier on the <5>Sudoku difficulty levels</5> hub, or head <6>home</6>.\"],\"OubwsB\":[\"How many puzzles are in the printable Newbie sudoku PDF?\"],\"P2bU2d\":[\"What makes a puzzle Easy\"],\"P6JVwt\":[\"Rarely. Most players can track the handful of candidates a hidden single needs in their head, but writing them down never hurts on a busier row.\"],\"PDbaU0\":[\"Do I need pencil marks for Newbie puzzles?\"],\"PFKt-9\":[\"Hard drops to \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues, and this is the first printable booklet on the site where subsets alone will not carry you to the end. Every puzzle in it was tested against a solver that already knows every intersection and every subset, and kept only because that solver stalled. What finishes them is a fish or a wing: the <0>X-Wing</0> and its larger and finned relatives, or one of the bivalue wing patterns.\"],\"PGxh1d\":[\"What is a finned fish in sudoku?\"],\"PKS4Or\":[\"Is the printable Infinity sudoku PDF free?\"],\"PYziuK\":[\"A chain has no fixed shape and is built link by link, which is far easier to track by writing each strong and weak link down than by scrolling a small screen.\"],\"PZQD8F\":[\"Play now\"],\"Pbm-BS\":[\"How does Suuudokuuu guarantee a tier’s technique requirement?\"],\"PdMLK1\":[\"Arto Inkala’s Everest (2012), 21 givens, published at SE 11.9.\"],\"Pg0uLs\":[\"Every level is free to play, with no ads and no sign-up. <0>Play a puzzle now</0> at any of the seven levels, or read the full breakdown of clue counts and required techniques on the <1>Sudoku difficulty levels</1> hub. Learning on paper? Start with the <2>printable Newbie sudoku PDF</2>.\"],\"PgRaz8\":[\"Play Easy Sudoku now\"],\"PivQ2i\":[\"Very. Every puzzle in the Infinity set has a published SE rating of at least \",[\"lowestRatingLabel\"],\", well past anything the generated tiers or the Hell corpus produce. Our own rater stops pricing the SE ladder at \",[\"SE_RATING_CEILING\"],\", so the figures quoted here come from independent raters, and our technique engine cannot finish any of these grids on its own. Expect to need long forcing chains and forcing nets, and expect a single puzzle to take far longer than anything else on this site.\"],\"Pqhtap\":[\"Easy\"],\"PrxlWP\":[\"Printable Easy Sudoku FAQ\"],\"PszyWW\":[\"What is the fastest way to get better at Sudoku?\"],\"PzS0uu\":[\"Hard boards carry \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues and are guaranteed to need at least one fish or wing pattern beyond every subset.\"],\"Q5B0cW\":[\"Hell\"],\"QBE_L9\":[\"<0>Nightmare.</0> Always stalls on fish and wings and always yields to chain or coloring logic.\"],\"Qo4hE6\":[\"A chain follows an alternating sequence of strong and weak links between candidates, starting from one end and reasoning outward until the two ends prove an elimination no matter which of them turns out to be true. X-Chain does this with a single digit; XY-Chain walks a path of bivalue cells instead, changing digit at every step. Simple coloring assigns two alternating colours to a network of strong links on one digit and clears any candidate that can see both colours. AIC folds all of them into one technique, mixing digits and link types along a single continuous chain. The difference from a fish or a wing is not subtlety but shape: a wing is a fixed arrangement of three or four cells you learn to recognise, while a chain has no fixed size and has to be built move by move. Nightmare is capped at AIC — anything that still resists is beyond what the generated tiers will hand you.\"],\"R1g33v\":[\"No puzzle, just the grid: one full-page 9×9 grid for copying out a puzzle from a book or newspaper, plus a second page of four smaller grids for quick practice sheets. Useful for teachers building their own worksheets or for anyone transcribing a puzzle they found somewhere without a printer-friendly version.\"],\"RJUjbN\":[\"Tips for pencil-mark solving\"],\"RMq7iB\":[\"A fish looks at one digit across several lines at once. The X-Wing is the smallest: a digit confined to the same two columns across two rows can be erased from the rest of those columns, because whichever row ends up holding it, the columns are already fixed. A <0>swordfish</0> stretches the same idea over three lines and a jellyfish over four. Finned and sashimi variants relax the base pattern by allowing one extra candidate that still supports a smaller, safe elimination once you account for it — and in our sample they fire far more often than the textbook shapes do. Wings work differently: an XY-Wing links three bivalue cells so a candidate shared between two of them can be erased wherever both can see, XYZ-Wing gives the pivot that candidate too, and W-Wing joins two matching bivalue cells through a strong link on one shared digit. Hard is capped at the W-Wing: a board that still will not move after every fish and wing has been tried is a Nightmare board, not a Hard one.\"],\"RRGDQM\":[\"Newbie is the easiest of Suuudokuuu’s seven tiers, followed by Easy, Medium, Hard, Nightmare, Hell and Infinity in increasing order of difficulty.\"],\"Rj2Y_n\":[\"The best-known Infinity grids have pages of their own, each playable, printable and solved step by step by the engine: <0>AI Escargot</0>, <1>Golden Nugget</1>, <2>Platinum Blonde</2>, <3>Everest</3>, <4>Kolk</4> and <5>Silver Plate</5>.\"],\"Rwv4vE\":[\"A forcing chain, on every board, layered on top of the chains, coloring, fish, wings and subsets the earlier tiers already require. X-Chain, XY-Chain, Simple Coloring and AIC will carry you far, but never all the way through; a <0>Nishio forcing chain</0> is the usual way to break the deadlock.\"],\"SPFeoH\":[\"Printable Hard Sudoku FAQ\"],\"ScJ9fj\":[\"Privacy policy\"],\"Sg-BY5\":[\"Clue count is not the difficulty. It is only the input: fewer starting digits mean fewer immediate placements, which forces the solver — human or machine — to reach for a wider set of named techniques before the grid moves again. Suuudokuuu strips digits from a solved grid down to a per-tier target, verifies the result still has exactly one solution, and then does the part that actually defines the tier: it solves the candidate twice, once with the technique ladder of the tier below and once with its own, and keeps the board only if the first solve fails and the second succeeds. Boards that miss are discarded and a fresh one is generated. That is why each tier above is stated as a guarantee rather than a hope. The <0>full technique index</0> lists every pattern that ladder contains, in the order a solver tries them. Within a band two boards can still differ a lot — <1>clues versus difficulty</1> measures exactly how much.\"],\"Sjq7vw\":[\"For each remaining blank cell, rule out every digit already used in its row, column and box. If exactly one digit is left, place it.\"],\"T5khAF\":[\"Play Hell Sudoku now\"],\"T91vKp\":[\"Play\"],\"TW-b-m\":[\"No. Clue count is only the input that forces a solver toward a wider technique set; the technique band the generator verifies is what actually defines each tier. The <0>clues versus difficulty guide</0> measures the gap directly.\"],\"T_JQXy\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Medium boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\".\"],\"T_R-Qz\":[\"Primary\"],\"TiHBaL\":[\"Hard Sudoku is a difficulty tier that starts at \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells and is defined by what a subset-only solver cannot finish: every board in the tier has been run through a solver equipped with every intersection and every subset up to the <0>hidden quad</0>, and kept only because that solver got stuck. What breaks the deadlock is a fish — <1>X-Wing</1>, <2>swordfish</2>, <3>jellyfish</3> and their <4>finned</4> and <5>sashimi</5> variants — or a wing: <6>XY-Wing</6>, <7>XYZ-Wing</7> and <8>W-Wing</8>.\"],\"TqC0fH\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, and every blank is reachable with a full house or a naked single.\"],\"U1U2tC\":[\"How many clues does an easy sudoku have?\"],\"U2AKxD\":[\"Printable sudoku FAQ\"],\"U9wBFD\":[\"Easy stays within singles-only logic, so it is still beginner-friendly. The only added skill over Newbie is spotting a digit that fits nowhere else in a unit.\"],\"UF5_iX\":[\"Default text size\"],\"UILsns\":[\"Write candidates into a cell only once scanning stops producing placements.\"],\"Umo747\":[\"No pencil marks, no elimination logic and no guessing are ever required.\"],\"Uq9L94\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, well under a third of the grid.\"],\"UveQZj\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Nightmare boards measures SE (Sudoku Explainer) \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\", with the <0/> as the most common hardest step. AIC is the ceiling here: every Nightmare board falls to it, and the <1>Hell tier</1> begins exactly where it stops, with boards that need a forcing chain. Some of those Hell boards carry more givens than Nightmare does, which is the clearest evidence on the site that clue count and difficulty are separate facts. The measured tables live in our <2>sudoku difficulty rating guide</2>. Qualitatively, this is where difficulty stops being about speed and becomes about holding an entire line of implication in your head without losing track of it.\"],\"V9j1Oq\":[\"No. Every board in the tier is verified solvable by the technique ladder up to AIC before it ships, so a completed chain always exists — finding it is the work.\"],\"VHv3Qz\":[\"Infinity puzzles carry \",[\"INFINITY_MINIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" to \",[\"INFINITY_MAXIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" clues and are checked for a single solution by two independent solving algorithms.\"],\"VT7jaN\":[\"A Hell board from the same verified corpus the app uses. Play it right here.\"],\"VUJcE0\":[\"Yes. Every puzzle in the booklet is solvable with a full house or a naked single alone, so no candidate marking or elimination logic is ever required.\"],\"Vmq46x\":[\"Once full houses and naked singles feel automatic, step up to the <0>printable Easy sudoku booklet</0>, which adds exactly one technique on top: the hidden single. To play Newbie puzzles on a screen instead, visit the <1>Newbie sudoku lander</1>. For the full technique ladder and the measured data behind these claims, see the <2>technique index</2> and the <3>sudoku difficulty rating guide</3>.\"],\"W1nEnp\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, a third of the grid filled in before you start.\"],\"W8o5ac\":[\"The other tiers are defined by the techniques they require. Infinity is defined by reputation, measured: a puzzle qualifies only if independent raters have published an SE rating of \",[\"minimumRatingLabel\"],\" or higher for it. Most of the \",[\"infinityCorpusSize\"],\" come from a 2011 snapshot of the hardest-puzzle database the sudoku-solving community maintains; the rest are the named classics, taken from the forum threads and publications where they first appeared. Before the set is packed into the app, a Dancing Links exact-cover solver and a bitmask solver both confirm that every grid has exactly one solution.\"],\"W9xBMf\":[\"New solvers should start at Newbie and move up one tier at a time; each step adds exactly one new technique over the tier before it, all the way up to Hard. See the <0>how to play guide</0> first if the three core rules are still unfamiliar.\"],\"WB-pGD\":[\"This booklet prints \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" of the hardest sudoku puzzles ever published, taken from Suuudokuuu’s Infinity tier: Arto Inkala’s Everest, AI Escargot, Platinum Blonde, Golden Nugget and other record grids, each with a published SE (Sudoku Explainer) rating between \",[\"lowestRatingLabel\"],\" and \",[\"highestRatingLabel\"],\". Every one has exactly one solution, and the solved grids are at the back.\"],\"WG8Ftb\":[\"How many clues does a Newbie puzzle have?\"],\"WTwN7-\":[\"Play \",[\"SITE_NAME\"]],\"WmW-Gm\":[\"Print space here matters more than at the easier tiers, because intersections and pairs work by marking candidates in the margins. The \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles print \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page at full cell size, leaving enough room around each digit to pencil in the small numbers an intersection or a pair reasons over. Solved grids close out the file so you can check your candidate marks against a confirmed answer. Our published sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Medium boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\" — numbers the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0> measures directly rather than assumes.\"],\"WqP4CN\":[\"Yes, in the iOS and Android apps. Once installed, \",[\"SITE_NAME\"],\" generates and solves puzzles entirely on your device, so it plays the same with no connection.\"],\"WrhTzj\":[\"Yes. Every difficulty booklet and the large-print set carry the full solved grids on the last pages, generated by the same solver that verifies every puzzle has exactly one solution before it ships.\"],\"WwMVff\":[\"How hard is Nightmare sudoku?\"],\"XGVJW3\":[\"Sudoku glossary\"],\"XORYRH\":[\"The \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles print \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page, sized so a chain crossing the whole grid still fits comfortably on one sheet. Full solved grids close the booklet, which matters more here than at the easier tiers — a single missed elimination partway along a chain compounds quickly, and a printed answer key catches it. The measured spread behind these claims lives in the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0>.\"],\"XpU6Tm\":[\"Why does Hell use a fixed puzzle corpus instead of generating puzzles?\"],\"XzG50N\":[\"Hell is Suuudokuuu’s hardest technique-graded tier — what most competitors call evil or extreme. A Hell board is defined by the reasoning it demands, not by how few clues it starts with: no Hell board can be finished with any technique Nightmare allows, so every one needs a forcing chain. Unlike the generated tiers, Hell is drawn from a bundled corpus of published hard puzzles, verified by two independent solvers before it ships, and every board still solves on our technique ladder without guessing. Expect to use every chain and coloring pattern first — <0>X-Chain</0>, <1>XY-Chain</1>, <2>simple coloring</2> and <3>AIC</3> — before a forcing chain breaks the deadlock.\"],\"Y3fLpk\":[\"How many puzzles are in the printable Hard sudoku PDF?\"],\"YGCzAJ\":[\"Every candidate board is solved twice: once with the tier below’s technique ladder, which must fail, and once with its own ladder, which must succeed. Boards that miss either test are discarded and regenerated.\"],\"YM-Le2\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, guaranteed to need at least one chain or coloring technique beyond every fish and wing.\"],\"Y_LLdr\":[\"Is the printable Easy sudoku PDF free?\"],\"Yj1j4Z\":[\"Puzzle 1 from the Hell booklet, one of \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" in the PDF.\"],\"YjxNca\":[\"Play Infinity Sudoku now\"],\"Z-7bqV\":[\"Hard Sudoku FAQ\"],\"Z9Mfy1\":[\"What is inside the booklet\"],\"Z9MhMF\":[\"What makes a puzzle Newbie\"],\"ZBT6Lr\":[[\"infinityCorpusSize\"],\" record puzzles with \",[\"INFINITY_MINIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" to \",[\"INFINITY_MAXIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" clues, published at SE \",[\"lowestRatingLabel\"],\" to \",[\"highestRatingLabel\"],\".\"],\"ZPXer3\":[\"Notes and candidates\"],\"Zm7CE_\":[\"Every technique \",[\"SITE_NAME\"],\" uses to generate hints is documented with a worked example board pulled straight from the solving engine. Start with the <0>full technique index</0>, or jump into one of the first patterns most players learn.\"],\"ZtZST0\":[\"Every puzzle needs a forcing chain, drawn from our bundled, verified Hell corpus. See the <0>Hell sudoku lander</0> to play it digitally.\"],\"_4AR-Z\":[[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PAGE_COUNT\"],\" pages\"],\"_YA7YX\":[\"Yes, along with Everest, Platinum Blonde and Golden Nugget. The booklet prints the puzzles as they were originally published.\"],\"_kK7k_\":[\"What is the difference between a wing and a chain?\"],\"_nkVQD\":[\"Nothing in the booklet needs a chain — that starts at the Nightmare tier.\"],\"_t9fa1\":[\"What is Infinity sudoku?\"],\"a3pVqb\":[\"Frequently asked questions\"],\"aF08Xt\":[\"Seven. Newbie, Easy, Medium, Hard, Nightmare and Hell form the technique ladder, each defined by a clue count and a guaranteed technique band rather than a marketing label. Infinity sits above them, a curated set of record puzzles chosen by published rating.\"],\"aIDRsS\":[\"<0>Medium.</0> Always stalls on singles and always yields to intersections and subsets — pointing pairs, box line reduction, naked and hidden pairs through quads.\"],\"aMv0h8\":[\"A Medium board from the same generator the app uses. Play it right here.\"],\"aOHWJD\":[\"<0>Naked Single</0> — a cell left with exactly one candidate.\"],\"aQ3vvP\":[[\"nightmareClueCount\"],\" clues, guaranteed to stall on wings and to yield to chains and coloring. See the <0>Nightmare sudoku lander</0> to play it digitally.\"],\"aeZiiA\":[\"Every puzzle guaranteed to have exactly one solution, no guessing required\"],\"agPptk\":[\"Medium\"],\"ajKnoT\":[\"The three rules of Sudoku\"],\"alOHPr\":[\"Ready for intersections and subsets to start mattering? Move on to the <0>printable Medium sudoku booklet</0>, or step back to <1>printable Newbie sudoku</1> for an even gentler grid. To play Easy puzzles on a screen instead, visit the <2>Easy sudoku lander</2>.\"],\"bIMckF\":[\"The standard PDF already uses a generous \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\"-puzzles-per-page layout. For bigger cells specifically, see the <0>printable Easy sudoku booklet</0>, which is also the source tier for our large-print PDF.\"],\"bJo3n2\":[\"Sudoku tips\"],\"bLowF0\":[\"Solving your first cells\"],\"bMqX8c\":[\"Scan for missing units\"],\"bQP2nt\":[\"Solving Easy boards without reaching for a hidden single? Step back to <0>Newbie Sudoku</0>, or step up to <1>Medium Sudoku</1>, where intersections and your first pairs appear. Prefer paper? Download the <2>printable Easy sudoku booklet</2>, or see the <3>sudoku for seniors</3> guide for large-print and comfort options. See the full <4>technique index</4>, the <5>how to play</5> guide, or every tier on the <6>Sudoku difficulty levels</6> hub back <7>home</7>.\"],\"bUGU7d\":[\"Size and shape. A wing is a fixed pattern of three or four cells you learn to recognise at a glance; a chain is built link by link and can run to any length, which is why chains sit a full band above wings on the SE scale.\"],\"bVG9Tb\":[\"Printable\"],\"bY8tm0\":[\"Source on GitHub\"],\"bc8DGE\":[\"Fill every empty cell with a digit from 1 to 9 so that no digit repeats in a row, a column or a 3×3 box.\"],\"c38U12\":[\"What is a pointing pair?\"],\"c3R2ID\":[\"Full House and Naked Single are the first two strategies Suuudokuuu’s solving engine tries on every board at every difficulty, because they are the cheapest deductions to verify. What sets Newbie apart is that the tier is defined as the boards that never need anything else. Strip more digits and a solver eventually stalls without hidden singles, intersections or subsets, and the generator throws those boards back rather than labelling them Newbie. If you can read a row and name the one digit missing from it, you already have every skill a Newbie puzzle asks for.\"],\"cJ_ZcY\":[\"Free Sudoku for iOS, Android and the web, offline in the apps\"],\"cK6miM\":[\"Difficulty\"],\"cVxfVr\":[\"No. Both techniques a Newbie puzzle requires can be read straight off the board, which is exactly why they are the fastest deductions in the game.\"],\"d4hJrp\":[\"Harder difficulty\"],\"d5hiJp\":[\"Why players stay\"],\"dKAb7E\":[\"Every Hell board needs a forcing chain: none can be solved with the techniques Nightmare allows, up to AIC.\"],\"dXoieq\":[\"Summary\"],\"do-_4n\":[\"At least one fish (<0>X-Wing</0> and its larger and finned relatives) or one bivalue wing pattern, on top of every intersection and subset the easier booklets already need.\"],\"dvRtE-\":[\"Seven: Newbie, Easy, Medium, Hard, Nightmare, Hell and Infinity. Hell puzzles come from a bundled, verified corpus of boards that each need a forcing chain, beyond anything Nightmare asks for, and <0>Infinity</0> serves record puzzles such as Everest and AI Escargot.\"],\"dyGlGe\":[\"The large-print set uses the same Easy-tier logic as the booklet above, but at \",[\"PRINTABLE_LARGE_PRINT_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" puzzles per page instead of \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\", so every cell and digit prints noticeably bigger. It suits low-vision solvers, classroom handouts read from a distance, and anyone who finds the standard grid cramped on paper. See the <0>large print sudoku page</0> for printing tips and the on-screen alternative, or the <1>sudoku for seniors</1> guide for the full comfort-focused rundown.\"],\"e0NrBM\":[\"Project\"],\"eBV_Xh\":[\"Nightmare boards carry \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues and are guaranteed to need at least one chain or coloring technique beyond every fish and wing.\"],\"eJ9n-i\":[\"New to the grid itself? Start with the <0>how to play guide</0> for the three rules and your first placements before picking a tier above.\"],\"eJum-4\":[[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles across \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PAGE_COUNT\"],\" pages, printed \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page with the solved grids at the back.\"],\"emFA81\":[\"Printable Nightmare Sudoku FAQ\"],\"enA4B7\":[\"Is Hard sudoku harder than Nightmare?\"],\"eo2JDj\":[\"Stuck on a puzzle?\"],\"eozBux\":[\"Not necessarily. Hell puzzles carry \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MINIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" to \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MAXIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" clues, drawn from a bundled corpus checked by two independent solving algorithms and filtered to boards that need a forcing chain, rather than generated fresh at print time.\"],\"ev-7sc\":[\"No. Hard tops out at the W-Wing; Nightmare starts where Hard stops and runs up to alternating inference chains. The two tiers are separated by a technique boundary, not by a clue count.\"],\"evANQd\":[\"Chain and coloring techniques: X-Chain, XY-Chain, simple coloring and AIC.\"],\"f0OFpM\":[\"<0>Hell.</0> Always stalls on chains and AIC and always needs a forcing chain, drawn from a bundled, verified corpus.\"],\"fRl01D\":[\"Printable sudoku\"],\"fUYszb\":[[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles, printed \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page, with a full solution key.\"],\"fY_UvT\":[\"This is the booklet to print for a short daily habit rather than a long sitting: fold it into a notebook, work one grid at a time, and there is never a candidate to write down or a pair to track across the row. It also suits a classroom introducing the rules for the first time, since a full class can finish a puzzle in the same short window without anyone stalling on an intersection they have not been taught yet. The \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\"-per-page layout still leaves each grid large enough to write in comfortably, even for a child’s handwriting, and the answer key at the back means a teacher never has to solve the sheet themselves to check it.\"],\"fiJRay\":[\"At least one <0>pointing pair</0>, <1>box-line reduction</1>, or a naked or hidden pair, on top of the singles the easier booklets already use. Nothing needs a fish, a wing or a chain.\"],\"g4WRV6\":[[\"hellCorpusSize\"],\" verified puzzles with \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MINIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" to \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MAXIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" clues, drawn from the tdoku 17-clue catalog and the magictour top1465 list rather than generated fresh.\"],\"g5Fk5U\":[\"Hard\"],\"gJOrtn\":[\"Difficulty levels\"],\"gh-p06\":[[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, guaranteed to stall on singles and yield to an intersection or a subset.\"],\"gmWGv_\":[\"A chain has no fixed shape, which is why marking it in pencil helps more here than at the easier tiers.\"],\"gqWp2B\":[\"A chain has no fixed shape: it is built link by link, and the only way to keep track of it is to write it down. On paper you can mark each strong and weak link as you go, follow the alternation to the far end, and see immediately which cells both ends can see. That is genuinely awkward on a phone screen you have to scroll. It is also the booklet where a wrong elimination compounds worst: mark a candidate as gone that should have stayed, and every link after it is unsound, so treat the solution pages as a real checkpoint rather than a formality.\"],\"h4IqRM\":[\"Comfortable spotting intersections and subsets? Move up to <0>Hard Sudoku</0>, where a fish or a wing is always required, or drop back to <1>Easy Sudoku</1> to revisit singles. Prefer paper? Download the <2>printable Medium sudoku booklet</2>. Browse the <3>technique index</3>, the <4>how to play guide</4>, every tier on the <5>Sudoku difficulty levels</5> hub, or head <6>home</6>.\"],\"h6WxWJ\":[\"Good for a relaxed solve\"],\"h7hJl_\":[\"How hard these puzzles are\"],\"hw66JY\":[\"Puzzle 1 from the Easy booklet, one of \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" in the PDF.\"],\"i0qMbr\":[\"Home\"],\"i7-8lN\":[\"Technique-aware hints that name the exact solving pattern, not just the next digit\"],\"iDOJbu\":[\"A fish spans whole rows or columns at once, which is easier to trace by marking a digit’s remaining positions down a printed column than by scrolling a screen. Wings need the opposite view — a few bivalue cells seen at a glance.\"],\"iEH6te\":[\"<0>Hidden Single</0> — a digit that only fits in one cell of a unit.\"],\"iggj45\":[\"How hard is Easy sudoku?\"],\"ippIMU\":[\"Those extra blanks over Newbie are enough that the grid stops filling itself in from <0>full houses</0> alone. Once the obvious placements run out, an Easy puzzle always leaves at least one cell where hidden single reasoning is the only way forward — check each unit’s missing digits against where they can still legally go, rather than reading candidates straight off one cell. Suuudokuuu’s technique engine tries hidden single third, right after full house and <1>naked single</1>, and an Easy-rated puzzle never needs to go further than that: no pointing pairs, no subsets, nothing that asks you to hold more than one unit in mind at once. The gap between the tiers is small on purpose — it is exactly one technique wide.\"],\"iu7tUI\":[\"Breadcrumb\"],\"iuw_bf\":[\"Difficulty rating\"],\"iyTmPq\":[\"Every named technique is a faster way of tracking the same row, column and box overlap across many cells at once.\"],\"j2fzAU\":[\"The SE ratings are the values independent raters and the sudoku-solving community publish. Suuudokuuu’s own rater reports \",[\"SE_RATING_CEILING\"],\" with a ceiling flag for anything harder than that, so it does not produce its own figure for these puzzles.\"],\"j2t1NI\":[\"Each tier links to a full page with a live puzzle preview and the honest difficulty facts from our <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0>. The PDF itself only ever needs a printer.\"],\"jFRHhT\":[\"<0>Infinity</0> — \",[\"infinityCorpusSize\"],\" of the hardest puzzles ever published, chosen by their published SE rating of \",[\"infinityLowestRating\"],\" to \",[\"infinityHighestRating\"],\" rather than by a technique band, and past the reach of every technique on the ladder.\"],\"jJ8CSk\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Hard boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\".\"],\"jMk3uh\":[\"Do not scan for the hardest cell first. Start by looking for the easiest possible placements, because clearing those first makes every later cell easier too.\"],\"jP5seF\":[\"Learn techniques in difficulty order rather than memorising every pattern at once. The <0>sudoku techniques index</0> lists them from full house up to the subset patterns, each with a worked example.\"],\"jmetfY\":[\"Do Easy puzzles ever need pencil marks?\"],\"juLzrc\":[\"Easy is the first tier where Suuudokuuu expects a genuine, if gentle, solve. An Easy board carries \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, a handful fewer than Newbie. Full houses and naked singles still clear most of the grid, but never all of it: at least one cell always needs a <0>hidden single</0>, where a digit fits only one cell of a row, column or box even though that cell still shows other candidates. That one extra pattern is the entire step up from Newbie to Easy, and it is a guarantee rather than a tendency: a board that a full-house-and-naked-single solver can finish is rejected as too easy for the tier, and a board that needs anything past the hidden single is rejected as too hard.\"],\"jwpEc6\":[\"Once the easy placements run out, tracking candidates by hand becomes essential. A candidate, sometimes called a pencil mark, is a digit that a cell could still legally hold based on what its row, column and box already contain. Writing every candidate into a cell — on paper as small numbers in the corner, or with the notes mode in an app — turns a puzzle that looks stuck into one where patterns become visible: pairs, triples and quads of candidates that repeat across a unit are exactly what techniques like naked pairs and hidden pairs are built to spot. The full method for every pattern lives in the <0>sudoku techniques index</0>, and every term used across these guides is defined in the <1>sudoku glossary</1>.\"],\"kFGAW9\":[\"Does a low clue count make these puzzles hard?\"],\"kV-GNp\":[\"<0>Medium</0> — \",[\"mediumClueCount\"],\" clues, guaranteed to stall on singles and to yield to intersections and subsets.\"],\"kbLXsu\":[\"Solutions included on the last pages\"],\"kc2u3T\":[\"Cross off candidates cell by cell\"],\"lAIHWp\":[\"<0>Hard</0> — \",[\"hardClueCount\"],\" clues, guaranteed to stall on subsets and to yield to fish and wing patterns.\"],\"lDdTS6\":[\"Printable Medium Sudoku FAQ\"],\"lINilK\":[\"The PDF opens with a cover page stating the puzzle and page counts, moves into \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles printed \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page, and closes with every solved grid on the final pages so answers never sit next to an unsolved puzzle. Every grid is drawn with vector lines and the standard PDF Helvetica font, so it stays sharp at any print size and never depends on a scanned image. Our published sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Newbie boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\" — numbers the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0> measures directly rather than assumes.\"],\"lPXkj-\":[\"Can I print this Newbie booklet in large print?\"],\"lQAsJI\":[\"<0>Column rule.</0> Each of the nine columns must contain the digits 1 to 9 exactly once each.\"],\"laMpeD\":[\"Nightmare\"],\"lxRnL8\":[\"<0>Box rule.</0> Each of the nine 3×3 boxes must contain the digits 1 to 9 exactly once each.\"],\"lzXj7Z\":[\"Every puzzle in this booklet needs a forcing chain: none can be finished with the techniques Nightmare allows, and each is drawn from our bundled and independently verified Hell corpus rather than generated fresh. Our published sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" boards measures the tier at SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\", with the <0/> as the most common hardest step. See the <1>17-clue guide</1> for why the clue count is not what makes them hard.\"],\"mDD4iI\":[\"Yes, with no account and no watermark, and every puzzle’s solved grid is included at the back.\"],\"mOCJOb\":[\"Cleared a few Nightmare boards? <0>Hell Sudoku</0> is the last tier, where every board needs a forcing chain. Step back to <1>Hard Sudoku</1> if fish and wings still feel unreliable. Prefer paper? Download the <2>printable Nightmare sudoku booklet</2>. Browse the <3>technique index</3>, the <4>how to play guide</4>, every tier on the <5>Sudoku difficulty levels</5> hub, or head <6>home</6>.\"],\"mVu64h\":[\"Newbie boards carry \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues and are guaranteed to finish with full houses and naked singles alone.\"],\"m_1uBm\":[\"Daily sudoku\"],\"mbw3Zs\":[\"What difficulty levels exist?\"],\"mdr9O2\":[[\"PRINTABLE_BLANK_GRID_PAGE_COUNT\"],\" pages\"],\"mf-vQH\":[[\"newbieClueCount\"],\" clues, solved with full houses and naked singles alone. See the <0>Newbie sudoku lander</0> to play it digitally.\"],\"mqvuZQ\":[\"Learn to solve\"],\"n8c99d\":[\"Sudoku solver\"],\"o83Dls\":[\"Easy boards carry \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues and are guaranteed to need at least one hidden single and nothing harder.\"],\"o8ErsC\":[\"Can a Sudoku have two solutions?\"],\"oACpQU\":[\"Difficulty guides\"],\"oF5_MF\":[\"Large text size\"],\"oFKMy-\":[\"Not ready for chains on paper yet? Step back to the <0>printable Nightmare sudoku booklet</0> for the same chain reasoning with more of the grid filled in, or to <1>printable Hard sudoku</1> for fish and wings without chain-length reasoning, or play Hell on a screen at the <2>Hell sudoku lander</2>, where the same corpus powers every puzzle. Ready for the record puzzles? The <3>printable Infinity sudoku booklet</3> prints Everest, AI Escargot and other record grids.\"],\"oH36ji\":[\"Do Infinity puzzles have a unique solution?\"],\"oQ8R9m\":[\"Do Nightmare puzzles ever need guessing?\"],\"oSfAuO\":[\"Medium Sudoku\"],\"o_ys4H\":[\"Every Newbie board is rated on the SE (Sudoku Explainer) scale the moment it is created. Our published sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Newbie boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\" — the very bottom of a scale that runs to 12, and below what most SE-based charts even bother to name. Newbie exists to teach the row-column-box overlap that every later technique builds on, not to test it. The measured range for this tier and every other is published in our <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0>. Treat a fast, mistake-free Newbie solve as confirmation you’re ready for Easy, not as a benchmark worth chasing for its own sake.\"],\"oc75Be\":[\"A well-formed Sudoku never does. If a puzzle has more than one valid completion it is considered broken, because logic alone can no longer point to a single answer.\"],\"ohi_6A\":[\"For each unit with several blank cells, check whether a digit that is still missing from the unit only fits in one of them, even if that cell has other candidates too.\"],\"p6O9l-\":[\"How many puzzles are in the printable Infinity sudoku PDF?\"],\"p95wx0\":[\"Full houses and singles as a baseline, plus pointing pairs, pointing triples, box line reduction and the naked or hidden subsets up to quads whenever singles run dry. At least one of those is always required, and nothing harder ever is.\"],\"pDFJMU\":[\"Download the PDF and open it in any PDF reader, then print at 100% scale on US Letter paper. Every grid is drawn with vector lines and standard PDF fonts, so there is nothing to rasterize and no quality loss at any print size.\"],\"pIksP6\":[\"Infinity Sudoku FAQ\"],\"pN5c2M\":[\"Nightmare Sudoku\"],\"pOHwnD\":[\"What techniques does this Medium booklet require?\"],\"pXows4\":[\"Suuudokuuu has seven difficulty levels: six that each require a wider set of techniques than the last, and Infinity.\"],\"pe908p\":[\"A clue, or given, is a digit printed on the board before you start. A candidate is a digit you are still considering for a blank cell, based on what its row, column and box currently rule out.\"],\"plp0e4\":[\"Play Nightmare Sudoku now\"],\"pu3rE1\":[\"At \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, this booklet is the first one worth solving with a pencil. Singles carry a Medium grid part of the way, but every puzzle in it provably stalls on them — that is the test each board had to fail to be printed here — until you spot a <0>pointing pair</0> or a <1>box-line reduction</1>, an intersection between a box and a line that only eliminates candidates, never places a digit outright. Nothing in the booklet needs a fish, a wing or a chain.\"],\"q7QiGX\":[\"How to play\"],\"qcBjCp\":[\"<0>Nightmare</0> — \",[\"nightmareClueCount\"],\" clues, guaranteed to stall on wings and to yield to chains and coloring.\"],\"qiqtfW\":[\"Play Medium Sudoku now\"],\"qrmik6\":[[\"PRINTABLE_LARGE_PRINT_SIZE\"],\" puzzles\"],\"qwJuVW\":[\"Footer\"],\"qyiPQ_\":[\"Easy is the booklet people reach for when they want to finish a puzzle without stopping to think hard about it — on a train, over a coffee break, or as a wind-down before bed. Every deduction still reads off the board rather than off a candidate grid, so there is rarely a reason to write a candidate in the margin; the hidden single asks you to scan a whole unit rather than one cell, which is a change of habit and not of difficulty. That makes it a natural size for printing several at once and working through a small stack over a week, since no single puzzle demands the concentration a Medium or Hard grid does.\"],\"r2FUkM\":[\"Play this puzzle here\"],\"r4WJmT\":[\"Sudoku techniques\"],\"r7ajsb\":[\"No ads, no account and no tracking inside the game, on the web or in the app\"],\"r8BZnz\":[\"Do I need pen and paper to solve Sudoku?\"],\"rFkWoz\":[\"No. Every puzzle Suuudokuuu generates is checked for a unique solution at generation time, so no cell ever requires a guess — and the bundled Hell-difficulty puzzles are additionally cross-checked by two independent solving algorithms, a Dancing Links exact-cover solver and a bitmask solver, before they ship. Any position that looks ambiguous just needs a technique that has not been tried yet.\"],\"rISE1w\":[\"What techniques do I need for Medium sudoku?\"],\"rUmdf8\":[\"Is the printable Hard sudoku PDF free?\"],\"rUv2wg\":[\"Also the source tier for the large-print PDF, sampled at \",[\"PRINTABLE_LARGE_PRINT_SIZE\"],\" puzzles.\"],\"rcYOQY\":[\"At least one chain or coloring technique — <0>swordfish</0>-level fish and <1>XY-Wing</1>-level wings are not enough on their own — on top of every fish and wing the Hard tier already needs.\"],\"rgh2Sh\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Nightmare boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\".\"],\"rhRptr\":[\"It is a real step up from Easy, but every technique it needs still works inside a single box or line at a time — the longer fish and chain patterns only start at Hard and beyond.\"],\"rjZpLn\":[\"Learn\"],\"rtx2YX\":[[\"easyClueCount\"],\" clues, and every puzzle needs at least one hidden single, never more. See the <0>Easy sudoku lander</0> to play it digitally.\"],\"sAlGDx\":[\"Free, open-source, no ads\"],\"sMgCJW\":[\"A board that needs a hidden single or anything harder is rejected and regenerated, never labelled Newbie.\"],\"sYhvIH\":[\"<0>Infinity.</0> The hardest sudoku puzzles ever published, such as Everest and AI Escargot, chosen by their published rating rather than a technique band — see the <1>Infinity lander</1>.\"],\"sZN9TU\":[\"Works fully offline once installed on iOS or Android\"],\"sf_Uq_\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Newbie boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\".\"],\"sgcKNN\":[\"Every Sudoku rule is really the same constraint applied to three different kinds of unit. Learn the constraint once and you already know all three rules.\"],\"sjwplg\":[\"Every booklet below is a free printable sudoku PDF built from the same puzzle sources the app plays — its generator and technique detectors, and for Hell and Infinity its bundled, verified corpora. Pick a difficulty for a \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\"-puzzle booklet with solutions on the last pages, or grab the large-print set or a blank sudoku grid below. No sign-up, no ads, no watermark.\"],\"ssPRl9\":[\"Suuudokuuu’s hardest tier: \",[\"infinityCorpusSize\"],\" of the hardest sudoku puzzles ever published, each with a published SE rating of \",[\"minimumRatingLabel\"],\" or more, playable for free with no ads.\"],\"svA7xQ\":[\"Ready for a puzzle that needs one more idea? Move up to <0>Easy Sudoku</0>, which adds the hidden single on top of everything here. Prefer paper? Download the <1>printable Newbie sudoku booklet</1>, or see the <2>sudoku for seniors</2> guide for large-print and comfort options. Browse the full <3>technique index</3> or the <4>how to play guide</4>, or head back <5>home</5> and see all seven tiers on the <6>Sudoku difficulty levels</6> hub.\"],\"szlBSl\":[\"Shareable puzzle links and move-by-move replays of your recent games, the last 20 per difficulty\"],\"tHJbOh\":[\"Is Infinity harder than Hell?\"],\"tK6SRc\":[\"Every puzzle needs a forcing chain, drawn from a bundled and independently verified corpus of boards with \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MINIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" to \",[\"HELL_CORPUS_MAXIMUM_GIVEN_COUNT\"],\" clues.\"],\"tYB68O\":[\"Puzzle 1 from the Infinity booklet, one of \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" in the PDF.\"],\"tc4WHX\":[\"Does a lower clue count always mean a harder puzzle?\"],\"thMLRg\":[\"Hard is capped at the W-Wing — a board that resists every fish and wing is graded Nightmare instead.\"],\"uFeI93\":[\"Each game reshuffles the grid, so a familiar record puzzle never looks the same twice.\"],\"uJerz5\":[\"Suuudokuuu grades its puzzles on a six-tier ladder, from Newbie through Hell, and each tier is defined by two concrete facts rather than a marketing label: how many clues the grid starts with, and which named solving techniques the tier is guaranteed to require. Every new board is also rated on the SE (Sudoku Explainer) scale the moment it is created, by the same open-source rating package the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0> uses to publish the measured band and SE range of every ladder tier below. Above the ladder sits <1>Infinity</1>, a curated set of record puzzles that carry the ratings independent raters publish, because they reach past the top of our own rating scale.\"],\"uy5vQS\":[\"Type or paste the grid into the <0>step-by-step sudoku solver</0> and it will name every move — Hidden Single, Naked Pair, X-Wing — instead of just filling the board in. It checks that your puzzle has exactly one solution first, and it runs entirely in your browser.\"],\"uyJsf6\":[\"About\"],\"v1_ToA\":[\"Intersections and pairs are found by marking every remaining candidate in a unit, so the layout leaves space in each cell specifically for those pencil marks.\"],\"vAJFgP\":[\"Good for a first sudoku habit\"],\"vEHxJQ\":[\"Sudoku difficulty levels\"],\"vLhN57\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Hard boards measures SE (Sudoku Explainer) \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\" — squarely in the range the solving community associates with fish and wing patterns, and well below the chain territory above 7. The most common hardest step is the <0/>, and the hardest anything in the sample reached is the <1/>. This is where casual solvers start reaching for a hint: fish and wings are easy to describe and genuinely hard to see on a live board, so expect a noticeably longer, more deliberate solve than Medium asks for. See the <2>sudoku difficulty rating guide</2> for the full per-tier data.\"],\"vNl4Yu\":[\"Easy starts at \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues, six below Newbie, and adds exactly one technique: every puzzle in this booklet needs at least one <0>hidden single</0>, and none of them needs anything harder. That single extra pattern is what makes this the booklet people print for a relaxed coffee-break solve rather than a teaching aid. It is also the source tier for our large-print PDF, sampled at \",[\"PRINTABLE_LARGE_PRINT_SIZE\"],\" puzzles for readers who want bigger cells.\"],\"vXIe7J\":[\"Language\"],\"vbOpg_\":[\"Why \",[\"SITE_NAME\"]],\"viJ4-_\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Hell boards measures SE \",[\"hellSeRatingRange\"],\".\"],\"vlNS-q\":[\"Newbie is Suuudokuuu’s beginner tier, the gentlest possible introduction to the grid. A Newbie board starts with \",[\"clueCount\"],\" of the 81 cells already filled. Every remaining cell can be found with the two simplest deductions in the game: a <0>full house</0>, where a unit is down to its last empty cell, and a <1>naked single</1>, where a cell’s row, column and box between them already account for eight of the nine digits. That is not a description of a typical Newbie board — it is the rule the generator enforces: a candidate board is only accepted as Newbie once a solver restricted to full houses and naked singles has finished it. No pencil marks, no elimination logic and no guessing are ever required.\"],\"voLlG5\":[\"How to start solving a Sudoku puzzle\"],\"vsge_o\":[\"New to Sudoku?\"],\"vvCT_r\":[\"Where to go next\"],\"vwz0Q4\":[[\"fileSizeKilobytes\"],\" KB PDF, US Letter\"],\"wIwe3l\":[\"How the ladder is built\"],\"wT9V53\":[\"Medium is where Suuudokuuu starts asking for pencil marks. A Medium board carries \",[\"clueCount\"],\" clues out of 81 cells, and singles alone provably never finish it: every board in the tier has been checked against a singles-only solver and rejected if that solver got through. Once full houses and singles run out, the puzzle stalls until you spot an intersection — a digit confined to where a box and a line overlap — or a pair locked together. <0>Pointing pairs</0>, <1>pointing triples</1> and <2>box line reduction</2> cover the intersections; <3>naked pairs</3> and <4>hidden pairs</4> cover the smallest subset pattern.\"],\"xI2Au1\":[\"Puzzle 1 from the Hard booklet, one of \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" in the PDF.\"],\"xRTkBI\":[\"Infinity\"],\"xTziZu\":[[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" puzzles across \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PAGE_COUNT\"],\" pages, \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page, with the solved grids at the back.\"],\"xYaf-9\":[\"Is Hell harder than Nightmare?\"],\"xkW-Mi\":[\"Why does this booklet leave more room around each digit?\"],\"xs4NvR\":[\"Is \",[\"SITE_NAME\"],\" free?\"],\"y-GOTe\":[\"After that, look at a single blank cell and cross off every digit that already appears in its row, its column and its box. If only one digit survives, that is a <0>naked single</0>, and it can be placed immediately. If a cell still has several candidates left, check whether one of those candidates cannot go anywhere else in the same unit — that is a <1>hidden single</1>, and it is just as safe to place. Together these two patterns solve most of an easy puzzle without any deeper reasoning.\"],\"yDLr5P\":[\"Large print sudoku\"],\"yNzy3T\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Medium boards measures SE \",[\"seRatingRange\"],\", and \",[\"singlesOnlyPuzzleCount\"],\" of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" finished on singles alone — this is the first tier where that number is zero by construction. The most common hardest step in the sample is the <0/>, and the hardest anything reached is the <1/>. Players who read pencil marks fluently clear a Medium board noticeably faster than players relying on mental candidate tracking, who will find this the first tier that genuinely rewards writing candidates down. The full per-tier data sits in our <2>sudoku difficulty rating guide</2>.\"],\"y_3zNL\":[\"Full houses and naked singles still clear most of the grid; the hidden single is the one addition over Newbie.\"],\"yjTW_5\":[\"What techniques do I need for Hell level?\"],\"yy8xD2\":[\"The grid itself never changes: nine rows, nine columns and nine boxes, eighty-one cells in total. What changes from puzzle to puzzle is only which cells start filled and which digits they hold, and it is that starting layout of givens that determines how much logic is needed to reach the one valid solution.\"],\"z0P0h9\":[\"Our sample of \",[\"sampleSize\"],\" Hell boards measures SE (Sudoku Explainer) \",[\"hellSeRatingRange\"],\", with the <0/> as the most common hardest step and the <1/> as the hardest step anything in the sample reached. Be careful not to read the clue count as the cause: the same sample puts <2>Nightmare</2> at SE \",[\"nightmareSeRatingRange\"],\" with \",[\"nightmareClueCount\"],\" clues, and some Hell boards start with more givens than that. This tier used to be built from 17-clue puzzles alone, and it rated no harder than Nightmare; selecting on the required technique instead is what separates the two. Our <3>clues versus difficulty guide</3> takes that argument apart properly, and the <4>rating guide</4> publishes the per-tier tables.\"],\"zGCYA8\":[\"Can I play AI Escargot and Everest here?\"],\"zX6n8C\":[\"Record puzzles such as Everest and AI Escargot, printed as originally published. See the <0>Infinity sudoku lander</0> to play them digitally.\"],\"zaRGXY\":[\"Blank sudoku grid\"],\"zdhNJO\":[\"Medium Sudoku FAQ\"],\"zu-XZL\":[\"Easy Sudoku\"],\"zuuvDj\":[[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE\"],\" record puzzles, printed \",[\"PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE\"],\" to a page, with a full solution key.\"]}")as Messages;